<!-- INTRO -->
<div class="intro">
  Over the last few years, Hegoa, operating between London and the Basque Country, has made significant strides in showcasing the obscure world of contemporary experimental and archival music emerging from the Basque region, an autonomous community in northern Spain with its own distinct cultural traditions and language. As can be seen here, the label works across various disciplines, including record releases, with a catalog already boasting 16 titles; radio, with programs on international stations such as NTS (London) and Dia! (Saint-Jean-de-Luz); and live music events, with performances at venues like Cafe OTO London, Kampai Bilbao, Kontenedora San Sebastián, and Bistrot St Esprit Bayonne. The label also works to recover archival video material, such as the documentaries on Llorenç Barber, "Sonar Ciudades," and on Jorge Oteiza, "Casa Vacía." All of this had a great impact on specialized media ranging from publications such as The Wire, The Quietus, AMA Artium, Basque on Decks, Soundohm, Berria, Eitb Kultura, Argia, Deia or Bidasoako Hitza among others.

</div>

<!-- CONTACT + GALLERY (placed below intro, above watch) -->
<div class="column">

  <div class="entry-block">
    <div class="section-title">contact</div>
    <div class="entries">
      <a href="mailto:hegoadiskak.eu@gmail.com">mail</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="entry-block">
    <div class="section-title">gallery</div>
    <div class="entries">
      <a href="https://www.instagram.com/hegoadiskak/?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        instagram
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

<!-- WATCH -->
<div class="entry-block">
  <div class="section-title">watch</div>
  <div class="entries">
    {% for item in collections.watch %}
      <a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.data.title }}</a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</div>

<!-- MAIN COLUMN -->
<div class="column">

  <div class="entry-block">
    <div class="section-title">catalog</div>
    <div class="entries">
      {% for item in collections.releases %}
        <a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.data.title }}</a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="entry-block">
    <div class="section-title">radio</div>
    <div class="entries">
      {% for item in collections.radio %}
        <a href="{{ item.data.external_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          {{ item.data.title }}
        </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="entry-block">
    <div class="section-title">live</div>
    <div class="entries">
      {% for item in collections.live %}
        <a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.data.title }}</a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="entry-block">
    <div class="section-title">read</div>
    <div class="entries">
      {% for item in collections.read %}
        <a href="{{ item.data.external_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          {{ item.data.title }}
        </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>

</div>
